---

Data: the route, split, rehearsal and transfer sets in data/tasks/ and the
measurement output in results/ are released under CC BY 4.0.

Those files are DERIVED from:

  - TwoHopFact (Yang, Gribovskaya, Kassner, Geva, Riedel, 2024; "Do Large
    Language Models Latently Perform Multi-Hop Reasoning?", ACL 2024), as
    distributed on the Hugging Face Hub as soheeyang/TwoHopFact under
    CC BY 4.0. The two-hop chains, their prompts and answers, and the entity
    aliases in the task files come from that dataset; it is not redistributed
    in full here.
  - Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), whose statements are released under
    CC0 1.0. The injected facts in the task files are Wikidata statements
    about the intermediate entities, retrieved through the Wikidata API.

The retention corpus used to measure held-out perplexity is the WikiText-2
test split (Merity et al., 2016; CC BY-SA 3.0), fetched at run time and not
redistributed here.

The per-item result files contain verbatim model outputs from Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct
(Apache 2.0) and Falcon3-3B-Instruct (Falcon-LLM licence), with email-like
strings the models generated replaced by a placeholder.

---

The archive as deposited on Zenodo is recorded as CC BY 4.0, which covers the
manuscript, documentation and derived data. The code is additionally available
under the MIT licence stated at the top of this file.
